.\" Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-sonnet-5-5
.Dd August 1, 2026
.Dt EMACS-COMPLETION-UX-RESEARCH 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm emacs-completion-ux-research
.Nd in-buffer completion UX — \(dqless annoying, more natural\(dq research
.Sh DESCRIPTION
\fBDate:\fP 2026-08-26 \fBScope:\fP A second round on the in-buffer side of
.Ql "lisp/init-completion.el" ,
narrowly aimed at the request \(dqmake the autocomplete popup and usage less annoying and more natural.\(dq
Builds on
.Ql "emacs-completion-research.7"
and the design in
.Ql "../design/completion.md" ;
the capf/keymap facts settled there are not re-litigated here.
\fBStatus:\fP Research + implementation.
The changes it motivates shipped in the same round in
.Ql "lisp/init-completion.el"
and
.Ql "test/completion-test.el" .
.Sh HOW TO READ THIS
Each concrete claim is tagged:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
\fB[V]\fP — verified against a primary source (package source read on its release branch, GNU manual, or NEWS).
.It
\fB[CFG]\fP — corroborated by a widely-cited real configuration, not by a normative source.
.It
\fB[FOLK]\fP — community consensus / folklore; sensible but not documented.
.It
\fB[I]\fP — a sound inference from a verified source.
.El
.Pp
Two hard constraints from the existing design bound every option below and are treated as non-negotiable: \fBTAB indents only\fP (R2) and \fBRET is a newline, never an accept\fP (R4).
.Sh 1. THE THREE LEVERS THAT WERE ACTUALLY AVAILABLE
The 2026-07 round left the trigger model (auto in code, manual in prose), the freed RET/TAB, and the capf chain settled.
What it did \fBnot\fP tune, and what this round found, are three orthogonal levers:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
\fBThe popup commits candidates you did not choose\fP —
.Ql "corfu-preview-current" .
.It
\fBThe popup fires half a beat too eagerly\fP —
.Ql "corfu-auto-delay"
/
.Ql "-prefix" .
.It
\fBTwo \(dqmore natural\(dq surfaces were simply absent\fP — a documentation panel
.No \&( Ns Ql "corfu-popupinfo" )
and inline ghost text
.No \&( Ns Ql "completion-preview-mode" ).
.El
.Pp
Nothing here needs a new package:
.Ql "corfu-popupinfo"
is a bundled corfu extension and
.Ql "completion-preview"
is built into Emacs 30+, so all three are
.Ql ":ensure nil"
and add nothing to the package closure.
.Sh 2. CORFU-PREVIEW-CURRENT — THE ACCIDENTAL-ACCEPT LEVER [V]
\fBFinding, and a corrected premise.\fP corfu's
.Ql "corfu-preview-current"
defaults to the symbol
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "insert" Ns No "\fP,"
not
.Ql "t" .
Its docstring: \fI\(dqIf the variable has the value
.No "`insert', the candidate is automatically inserted on further input.\(dq\fP So with the shipped default, while a popup is open, \fBcontinued typing commits the selected candidate\fP into the buffer. [V — corfu.el defcustom]"
.Pp
This directly undercuts the spirit of R4 and the freed RET/TAB.
The 2026-07 design took great care that RET, TAB, and continued typing never \fIaccept\fP a candidate — but
.Ql "corfu-preview-current insert"
was quietly doing exactly that on continued input.
Setting it to
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "nil" Ns No "\fP"
shows the menu with no inline text and inserts nothing until an explicit
.Ql "corfu-complete"
.No \&( Ns Ql "C-M-i" ).
[V — docstring; CFG — this is what Prot's config sets]
.Pp
This is the single biggest \(dqless annoying / more natural\(dq win, and it is also what makes room for lever 3: with
.Ql "nil" ,
corfu contributes \fBno\fP inline text, so
.Ql "completion-preview-mode" Ns No "'s"
ghost is the one and only inline surface — no duelling previews.
.Pp
\fBShipped:\fP
.Ql "(corfu-preview-current nil)"
in the corfu
.Ql ":custom"
block.
.Sh 3. AUTO-POPUP TIMING — THE EAGERNESS LEVER [V]
\fBCorrected premises.\fP corfu's shipped defaults are
.Ql "corfu-auto-delay"
= \fB0.2\fP and
.Ql "corfu-auto-prefix"
= \fB3\fP.
[V — corfu.el / GNU ELPA doc] This config was running \fB0.1 / 2\fP — \fIbelow both defaults\fP, in the direction corfu's own docstrings caution against: a very short delay or small prefix \(dqwill create high load for Emacs, in particular if executing the completion backend is costly,\(dq and the README example annotates
.Ql "corfu-auto-delay 0"
/
.Ql "corfu-auto-prefix 0"
with \(dqTOO SMALL — NOT RECOMMENDED!\(dq.
[V — corfu README + docstrings]
.Pp
The 2026-07 design was explicit that 0.1 / 2 were \fBnot measured\fP — \(dqevery number in circulation for this stack is folklore until measured.\(dq
Given no measurement exists either way, moving to corfu's \fIdocumented defaults\fP (0.2 / 3) is the better-justified resting point than sitting below them: it is the one change most directly aimed at \(dqit pops up while I'm still typing,\(dq and it aligns the popup with
.Ql "completion-preview-minimum-symbol-length"
(3), so the ghost text and the popup begin suggesting at the same keystroke.
[V for the defaults; I for \(dqbetter-justified than 0.1/2\(dq]
.Pp
Real configs cluster at delay 0.1–0.25 and prefix 2–3; anything at or above 0.2 / 3 is squarely inside the documented-safe range, below it is the debated zone.
Prot side-steps the question entirely (no auto-popup).
[CFG]
.Pp
\fBShipped:\fP defaults raised to
.Ql "jotain-completion-auto-delay 0.2" ,
.Ql "jotain-completion-auto-prefix 3" ,
with the docstrings rewritten to cite the corfu recommendation instead of \(dqnot tuned.\(dq
.Sh 4. CORFU-POPUPINFO — THE DOCUMENTATION PANEL [V]
\fBWhat it is.\fP A bundled corfu extension (successor to
.Ql "corfu-doc" )
that shows a child-frame panel beside the candidate list with the selected candidate's docstring or source location — the IDE \(dqdetail pane.\(dq
Enabled with
.Ql "(corfu-popupinfo-mode 1)" ;
inactive by default like all corfu extensions.
[V — extensions/corfu-popupinfo.el + corfu README]
.Pp
\fBDelay is a cons
.Ql "(INITIAL . SUBSEQUENT)" Ns No ",\fP"
defaulting to
.Ql "(2.0 . 0.5)" :
a long wait before it first appears (so docs do not flash on every pause) and a short refresh as you arrow between candidates.
The split exists precisely to make first appearance unobtrusive while keeping candidate-to-candidate refresh instant.
A responsive-but-quiet value is
.Ql "(1.0 . 0.5)"
(Prot uses
.Ql "(1.25 . 0.5)" ).
[V — defcustom; CFG — Prot]
.Pp
\fBKeymap safety.\fP
.Ql "corfu-popupinfo-map"
binds only
.Ql "M-t"
(toggle),
.Ql "M-h" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "M-g"
(documentation/location), and the
.Ql "C-M-v"
scroll family.
It touches \fBneither\fP the freed RET/TAB \fBnor\fP
.Ql "M-n" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "M-p" ,
so it is safe under this config's constraints — verified against the full
.Ql "corfu-map"
list.
[V]
.Pp
.Ql "corfu-echo"
(one-line echo-area doc,
.Ql "corfu-echo-delay '(2.0 . 1.0)" )
is the lighter alternative; running both is redundant.
This config chose the panel for the fuller IDE feel; the echo mode is the documented fallback if the child frame ever feels heavy.
[V — extensions/corfu-echo.el; FOLK — \(dqpick one\(dq]
.Pp
\fBShipped:\fP
.Ql "corfu-popupinfo"
block, delay
.Ql "(1.0 . 0.5)" ,
gated by
.Ql "jotain-completion-doc-popup"
(default t).
.Sh 5. COMPLETION-PREVIEW-MODE — INLINE GHOST TEXT (FINDING 12B) [V]
This is the deferred feature decision from
.Ql "emacs-nix-deep-review.7"
Finding 12, option (b): adopt the built-in inline preview alongside corfu.
.Pp
\fBWhat it is.\fP A buffer-local minor mode (Emacs \fB30.1\fP; user options extended in \fB31\fP) that draws the top completion candidate as greyed \(dqghost text\(dq after point, updated as you type, sourced from the \fBsame\fP
.Ql "completion-at-point-functions"
corfu uses — so it previews the eglot/cape/tempel candidates already configured, with no separate source list.
.Ql "global-completion-preview-mode"
is the global twin.
[V — NEWS.30 \(dqNew Modes and Packages\(dq; completion-preview.el commentary]
.Ss 5.1 The R2 landmine [V — decisive]
.Ql "completion-preview-active-mode-map"
(active only while a preview shows) binds, verbatim on the
.Ql "emacs-31"
branch:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
"C-i" #'completion-preview-insert
"M-i" #'completion-preview-complete
.Ed
.Pp
.Ql "C-i" ,
.Ql "TAB" ,
and
.Ql "?\et"
are the \fBsame event\fP in Emacs —
.Ql "\(dqC-i\(dq"
and
.Ql "\(dqTAB\(dq"
are identical keymap keys.
So the shipped binding \fBis\fP \(dqTAB accepts the preview\(dq: on a terminal the Tab key sends
.Ql "C-i"
directly; in a GUI the
.Ql "<tab>"
event is translated to
.Ql "C-i"
by
.Ql "local-function-key-map"
when
.Ql "<tab>"
is unbound in the active maps, and the minor-mode map then shadows
.Ql "indent-for-tab-command" .
The mode's commentary confirms the intended UX is \(dqaccept with TAB.\(dq
Left as-is this is a \fBdirect R2 violation\fP in exactly the buffers it runs in.
[V — keymap source + Emacs key-translation semantics]
.Pp
The remedy is a one-liner:
.Ql "(keymap-unset completion-preview-active-mode-map \(dqC-i\(dq t)"
(REMOVE = t), after which Tab falls through to indentation while a preview shows.
The whole-candidate accept then needs a non-TAB home; this config binds
.Ql "completion-preview-insert"
to
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "M-RET" Ns No "\fP"
(R4 governs bare RET only;
.Ql "M-RET"
is a distinct event) and leaves
.Ql "M-i"
(common-prefix complete) as shipped.
[V —
.Ql "keymap-unset"
semantics; I — M-RET is R4-safe]
.Pp
\fBDo not\fP copy the common community recipe that binds TAB to
.Ql "completion-preview-complete"
(e.g. the \(dqÀ la Mode\(dq corfu+preview config): it re-introduces the exact R2 violation.
[FOLK, explicitly incompatible with R2]
.Pp
\fBR4 is safe out of the box\fP — the map binds no
.Ql "RET" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "<return>" ,
not even commented out.
The only obligation is: do not add one.
[V]
.Ss 5.2 The options that matter [V — all defaults from the emacs-31 source]
.Bd -literal -offset indent
| Option | Default | Use here |
| completion-preview-idle-delay | nil (immediate) | Set to jotain-completion-auto-delay (0.2) so the ghost and the popup share one debounce, and a costly LSP capf is not hit twice per keystroke at different times. |
| completion-preview-minimum-symbol-length | 3 | Left as-is; matches the 3-char popup prefix. (nil would fire after punctuation/whitespace too — more aggressive, not less.) |
| completion-preview-sort-function | #'minibuffer--sort-by-length-alpha (user option in 31) | Paired with corfu-sort-function so the ghost matches the popup's top row — NEWS.31 promotes it as a user option specifically "together with … Corfu … for a more integrated experience." Guarded on the option's custom-type so Emacs 30 is untouched. |
| completion-preview-inhibit-functions | nil (new in 31) | Add a comment/string predicate ((nth 8 (syntax-ppss))) so the ghost does not appear where symbol completion is meaningless. Guarded on boundp (absent on 30). |
| completion-preview-completion-styles | '(basic) — a defvar, not a defcustom | Left as shipped. The preview computes candidates with basic (prefix) matching, not the config's orderless. Consequence: the ghost is prefix-only, which is the conservative, predictable choice for an always-on inline hint; orderless stays where it belongs, in the popup and the minibuffer. [V — it is a defvar defaulting to (basic); I — leaving it prefix-only is the calmer choice] |
.Ed
.Ss 5.3 Coexistence with corfu, and where to run it [V + FOLK]
corfu has \fBno\fP inline ghost text of its own; it previews only inside its popup
.No \&( Ns Ql "corfu-preview-current" ).
The corfu README does not mention completion-preview — they are independent, rendering in different places (popup vs. inline overlay), and do not fight over one UI element.
They \fIdo\fP both read the same capf, so with both surfaces live you see the popup list \fBand\fP one ghost line.
[V]
.Pp
The folklore worry about a \(dqbusy double surface\(dq comes almost entirely from running completion-preview together with
.Ql "corfu-preview-current insert"
— i.e. \fItwo\fP inline previews.
Setting
.Ql "corfu-preview-current nil"
(§2) collapses that to exactly one inline surface (the ghost) plus the popup list — which is the familiar modern-editor arrangement, not noise.
[I from §2 + the coexistence facts]
.Pp
\fBPlacement decision.\fP Rather than
.Ql "global-completion-preview-mode"
(which would put ghost text in prose and the minibuffer — the minibuffer is explicitly \fInot\fP recommended, and prose is meant to stay quiet per R1), the mode is enabled only in
.Ql "jotain-completion-auto-modes"
— the \fIsame\fP mode list that gets the auto-popup.
Code gets both surfaces; prose inherits neither and stays manual-only via
.Ql "C-M-i" ;
the minibuffer is never touched.
[FOLK for \(dqrun preview where auto-popup is on\(dq; V for the minibuffer caveat — minad/vertico discussion #512]
.Pp
\fBShipped:\fP
.Ql "completion-preview"
block enabled across
.Ql "jotain-completion-auto-modes" ,
gated by
.Ql "jotain-completion-inline-preview"
(default t), with the C-i unbind, the M-RET accept, the idle-delay pairing, the sort pairing, and the comment/string inhibit.
.Ss 5.4 Residual — needs eyes on a GUI [I]
Two things batch tests cannot settle, recorded honestly, same as the 2026-07 design did for
.Ql "corfu-complete" Ns No "'s"
feel:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
Whether ghost + popup together feels integrated or busy in day-to-day coding.
Mitigated structurally
.No \&( Ns Ql "corfu-preview-current nil" ,
matched sorts) and by the one-toggle opt-out
.Ql "jotain-completion-inline-preview" .
.It
Whether prefix-only ghost (from
.Ql "completion-preview-completion-styles '(basic)" )
ever disagrees jarringly with an orderless popup top row.
If so, the lever is aligning that defvar with
.Ql "completion-styles" ,
at the cost of a fuzzy ghost.
.El
.Sh 6. OPTIONS CONSIDERED AND NOT TAKEN
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "corfu-preselect 'prompt" Ns No "\fP"
— would keep typed input selected so an accidental accept inserts your own text.
With
.Ql "corfu-preview-current nil"
already removing auto-insert, the marginal safety is small and it complicates accepting the first candidate; left at the default
.Ql "valid" .
[V — defcustom; decision: out of scope]
.It
\fBBuffer-local
.Ql "orderless-literal-only" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "basic"
style for corfu\fP (the README's \(dqseparate styles for minibuffer vs. Corfu\(dq recipe) — a real \(dqmore predictable in-buffer matching\(dq lever, but it changes matching semantics the owner has been living with and is orthogonal to \(dqannoying popup.\(dq
Deferred as a separate decision, not bundled into this round.
[V — README recipe]
.It
.No "\fB" Ns Ql "corfu-on-exact-match" Ns No "\fP"
— already
.Ql "nil"
(no surprising auto-insert); no change.
[V]
.It
\fBWidth-pinning
.No \&( Ns Ql "corfu-min-width" Ns No "/" Ns Ql "-max-width" )
and hiding the scrollbar\fP — cosmetic calm-feel tweaks; not \(dqannoying-usage\(dq fixes.
Left alone.
[CFG]
.El
